# Windsurf Rules — Pardix Browser

## Project
Flutter mobile browser (Android/iOS). Package: `com.dino.pardix`. Flutter ^3.10.0.
Architecture: Clean Architecture + flutter_bloc.

## Architecture Layers
```
core/          → shared utilities, never import from features/ or presentation/
domain/        → pure Dart, zero Flutter/third-party dependencies
data/          → implements domain contracts (repositories, services)
features/      → self-contained modules (each has bloc/ widgets/ services/)
presentation/  → top-level screens (HomePage is the root screen)
```
Import rule: presentation → features → domain ← data

## BLoC Pattern
- Feature state = BLoC only (no widget setState for feature data)
- Events: NounVerbEvent (TabAddEvent, DownloadStartEvent)
- States: Equatable, Freezed for sealed unions
- BLoC access: context.read<XBloc>() only at top level, pass callbacks downward

## Required Before Every Commit
```bash
flutter analyze           # zero errors
dart format lib/          # formatted
flutter test              # all pass
# If .freezed source changed:
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
```

## Style Rules
- snake_case files, PascalCase classes, camelCase methods/vars, _underscore private
- Colors → AppColors | Strings → AppStrings | Sizes → AppSizes
- Storage → StorageService only (never raw SharedPreferences)
- HTTP → ApiClient only (never raw Dio)

## Logging (lib/core/logger/app_logger.dart)
Never use print() or the deprecated Logger class.

```
AppLogger.verbose / .debug / .info / .warning / .error / .fatal
AppLogger.event(AnalyticsEvent.*, params: {AnalyticsParam.*: value})
```

Routing in release: INFO→breadcrumb, WARNING→breadcrumb+non-fatal, ERROR→non-fatal, FATAL→fatal, .event()→Analytics
Tag = class name: 'TabBloc', 'WebView', 'Download', 'Search', 'Storage'
Never call FirebaseCrashlytics or FirebaseAnalytics directly — always go through AppLogger

## Do Not Touch
- packages/flutter_inappwebview/ — local fork with custom patches
- *.freezed.dart / *.g.dart — generated files
- android/.key.properties / *.jks / google-services.json — secrets

## Key Entry Points
- App start: lib/main.dart
- Main UI: lib/presentation/pages/home/home_page.dart
- WebView: lib/features/webview/widgets/webview_page.dart
- Tab state: lib/features/tabs/bloc/tab_bloc.dart
